  "report_period": "Week 17 (17th Apr to 24th Apr 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Post Panamax \"Corona Brave\" 88/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS 12/2027, DD 11/2026) of Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha was committed to Chinese interests at USD 12,9 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Royal Award\" 88/2007 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 02/2027) was sold in February at USD 11,5 mill. Greek owners committed the Kamsarmax \"Skyros\" 79/2011 Nanjing, China (SS/DD 12/2026) at high USD 13 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older \"Giewont\" 79/2010 New Century, China (SS 01/2030, DD 12/2027) was sold in March at USD 11,7 mill. Iason Hellenic Shipping committed the Panamax \"Alexandros Petrakis\" 76/2008 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 13,3 mill. Note that the one-year-younger \"Agri Kinsale\" 77/2009 Oshima, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 15,1 mill. Moreover, the \"Donousa\" 76/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2027) of Dileton Maritime was committed at USD 9,6 mill, while the one-year- younger \"Ocean Lion\" 75/2005 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2028) was sold in early March at USD 10 mill. The Ultramax \"Amstel Tiger\" 60/2016 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 08/2026) of Triton Navigation was committed at high USD 26 mill. Note that a couple of months ago, the one-year-younger \"Only You\" 60/2017 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) was sold at USD 28,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Japanese owners committed the OHBS \"Phoenix K\" 54/2007 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 05/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 14 mill, a noticeable increase from the last done, the one-year-younger \"Mercury Ocean\" 53/2008 Iwagi, Japan, earlier this month at USD 13 mill. In addition, Seamax Marine committed the \"Asteris\" 53/2007 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 04/2027) at USD 9,8 mill. Remind you that back in January, the sister vessel \"MDM Bromo\" 53/2007 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 07/2027) was sold at USD 8,1 mill.",
    "tankers": "Greek owner Petrochem General Management has acquired the LR1 \"Danship Tope\" 76/2008 Dalian, China (SS 03/2028, DD 06/2026) for USD 19 mill. Note that the sellers bought the vessel in January under the name \"Pelagic Tope\" with DD due 03/2026, at USD 13,8 mill. VOSCO have committed their MR2 \"Dai Phu\" 50/2006 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 08/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 13,3 mill, while the \"Optimal Ace\" 50/2006 Stx, Korea (SS 01/2031, DD 07/2028) was committed a week ago at USD 16,5 mill. The MR1 \"Easterly Canyon\" 36/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 07/2029, DD 06/2027) was committed to Greek interests at USD 19 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"HTM Everest\" 37/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea, (SS 03/2030, DD 03/2028) was sold back in January at USD 20 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the Singapore-Japan range were reported at usd 18,000/21,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into South East Asia and India were fixed at levels ranging from usd 20,000/24,000 pd. South East Asia trips via Indonesia into India and South East Asia were reported around usd 21,000/23,000 pd. South China trips into India and Singapore-Japan range were fixed at usd 18,000/20,000 pd. North China trips via Russian Far East into India were reported at usd 20,500 pd. East Coast South American trips into the Singapore-Japan range were fixed between usd 18,000/22,000 pd. Additionally, North Coast American trips into the Singapore-Japan range were fixed in a range of usd 23,000/25,000 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed at usd 21,850 pd for 2 or 3 laden legs.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from East Coast India into China were fixed at usd 18,500 pd, while South Africa trips into South East Asia were reported at usd 16,500 pd with a ballast bonus of usd 165,000. On the period front, an Ultramax was reported fixed at usd 19,250 pd for 4/6 months.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Atlantic, Continent trips into the US Gulf were fixed at usd 14,000 pd, while trips from the Continent into the Mediterranean were reported at usd 17,000 pd. East Mediterranean trips into West Africa were fixed at usd 12,000 pd."
    }
  },
